     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,32,96);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\">hi all,</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,32,96);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\"> we found a bug in oSCR yesterday in the way it was handling the trap operation matrix. This only affects things if you were using the data2oscr function to convert EDF and TDF format data into the oSCR scrFrame structure.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,32,96);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\"> In any case, you can update directly from GitHub by doing this:</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,32,96);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,32,96);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\">install.packages(&quot;githubinstall&quot;)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,32,96);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\">install.packages(&quot;devtools&quot;)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,32,96);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\">library(githubinstall)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,32,96);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\">library(devtools)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,32,96);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,32,96);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\">#install <span>oSCR</span> directly from github<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,32,96);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\">install_github(&quot;jaroyle/<span>oSCR</span>&quot;)<u></u><u></u></span></p></div>\r\n"
